  "hostNotes": "Accept any Arnott's line, savoury crackers and crispbreads included (Arnott's calls them all biscuits), plus classic bakery/CWA biscuits like Anzac, Yo-Yo, Melting Moment and Jam Drop. Flavour variants collapse to the parent (Double Coat -> Tim Tam, Chicken Crimpy -> Shapes); a bare 'Monte' or 'shortbread' means Monte Carlo and Shortbread Cream respectively unless the player clarifies; Savoy and Jatz are the same biscuit under different state names but are scored separately unless the host rules otherwise. Traps: Lamingtons, Vanilla Slice, Chocolate Crackles, Honey Joys and Fairy Bread are not biscuits; Afghans, Toffee Pops, Squiggles, Mallowpuffs and Griffin's are New Zealand; Oreo, Hobnob, Custard Cream and Jammie Dodger are not Aussie; 'Assorted Creams' or 'Family Assorted' is a pack, so ask the player to name one biscuit from it."
}
